.TH DEBFED 1 "September 2026" "debfed" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
debfed \- install Debian-targeted applications on Fedora as native RPMs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B debfed
.I COMMAND
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIARGS\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B debfed
converts vendor-distributed
.I .deb
application packages into native RPMs and installs them through dnf, so
the application is owned by rpm, appears in
.BR "rpm \-qa" ,
and is removable with
.BR dnf .
No container, chroot or virtual machine is involved.
.PP
Debian's
.B Depends:
field is discarded. Requirements are derived instead from the payload's
ELF headers using rpm's own dependency generator, which emits
capabilities in Fedora's native syntax; SONAMEs are identical across
distributions where package names are not.
.PP
.B debfed
is not a general Debian-to-Fedora converter. Base system packages,
kernel modules, and packages requiring dpkg semantics are refused with a
stated reason.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI inspect " DEB..."
Report requirements, chosen strategy and any refusals. Read-only.
.TP
.BI build " DEB"
Produce an RPM without installing it.
.TP
.BI install " DEB"
Convert and install. A dnf transaction preview is always shown first.
.TP
.BI remove " NAME"
Remove an installed package via dnf.
.TP
.B map
View and edit the dependency mapping database.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable output (\fBinspect\fR only).
.TP
.B \-\-offline
Skip dnf resolution. No strategy will be chosen.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Stop after the transaction preview (\fBinstall\fR only).
.TP
.B \-y ", " \-\-yes
Skip the confirmation prompt. The dry run still runs.
.TP
.BI \-\-map\-file " PATH"
Additional mapping database, taking highest precedence.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/debfed/mappings.yaml
User dependency mappings, overriding the shipped database.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Package refused, or user aborted.
.TP
.B 2
Error reading the package or running a required tool.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dnf (8),
.BR rpm (8),
.BR rpmbuild (8)
